# 8x11 BACK view of the typing pose, frame 0 — the desk pose of a back-turned
# agent mid tool-call.
#
# Body is `seated_back`; only the ARMS move, and they move exactly as
# `typing_0.sprite`'s do (left hand down at row 10). Keeping the two frame pairs
# in lockstep is what makes a back-turned typist read as the SAME action as a
# front-facing one — before this existed, every back-turned agent fell back to
# the still `seated_back` and a working desk was indistinguishable from an idle
# one on half the office.
@frame 0
@mark head.back 4 2
. n H H H H n .
n H H H H H H n
H H H H H H H H
H H H H H H H H
. H H H H H H .
. n H H H H n .
. B B B B B B .
B B B B B B B B
B B B B B B B B
S B B B B B B .
. . . . . . S .
